  steps: [
    { math: '1 · Dopamine: wanting, not liking', note: 'Dopamine signals prediction and motivation — it drives SEEKING. Addictive drugs spike it unnaturally, and the system recalibrates (tolerance): the circuit wants more, enjoys less. Berridge\'s distinction: dopamine is "wanting"; opioids are "liking".' },
    { math: '2 · Serotonin: mood and more', note: 'SSRIs (Prozac) raise synaptic serotonin — helping depression within weeks, though the mechanism is subtler than "low serotonin = sad". Also gates sleep, appetite and gut function (95% of body serotonin is in the gut).' },
